codex
The public runner calls `setup` outside each per-MLP `BudgetContext`, so precomputing directions there is valid. The fixed term in `_sample_count` is therefore conservative for the setup path, but higher budget fractions still worsened officially, so I’m not forcing more samples blindly.
codex
Because setup is outside the per-MLP budget, there may be a little unused compute headroom in the sample-count heuristic. A full 0.2 fraction was too much, but I’m testing a modest increase to 0.11 with the best correction value.
